Zero-copy display with tiled buffers: the module option tiled_scanout=1 makes
the primary planes advertise, besides linear, GFX11's 256 KiB and 64 KiB R_X
swizzles without DCC for every count of pipes and packers.

A host that reads the layout of the guest's scanout buffer from its amdgpu
metadata (the qemu-gui fork's QEMU_SDL_ZC_TILED=explicit) can put tiled
buffers on its screen as they are.  Without modifiers on the planes the
compositor's buffers are tiled already, but a fullscreen client's are then
allocated with modifiers the plane does not list, and the compositor
composites it instead of scanning it out: +2.7 ms key to screen on the
laptop (2026-10-03).  With linear_scanout=1 everything is linear instead,
which costs the compositor and the copy path.  This list lets guest Mesa
pick the tiled layout of its GPU (it ignores the entries of other GPUs) for
both.  DCC stays out: its planes would have to be passed along.  The cursor
plane keeps linear only.  Read at probe (0444): a kernel argument.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-03 03:40:21.044850993 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-03 03:40:21.046417253 +0200
@@ -105,6 +105,18 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(linear_scanout, "Advertise the linear modifier, so that scanout buffers are linear (zero-copy display, default 0)");
 module_param_named(linear_scanout, virtio_gpu_modparam_linear_scanout, int, 0444);
 
+/*
+ * Zero copy with tiled buffers: a host that reads the layout from the
+ * buffer's amdgpu metadata (the qemu-gui fork) can show tiled buffers too.
+ * The primary planes then also advertise the tiled layouts that guest Mesa
+ * may choose for the GPU (see virtio_gpu_scanout_modifiers), so that the
+ * compositor's buffers and a fullscreen client's stay tiled and the latter
+ * can still go to the plane directly.  Read at probe: a module option.
+ */
+int virtio_gpu_modparam_tiled_scanout;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(tiled_scanout, "Advertise tiled AMD layouts (GFX11 R_X, no DCC) on the primary planes besides linear, for a host that reads the layout from the buffer (zero-copy display, default 0)");
+module_param_named(tiled_scanout, virtio_gpu_modparam_tiled_scanout, int, 0444);
+
 static ktime_t virtio_gpu_vblank_interval(struct virtio_gpu_output *output)
 {
 	/* 60 Hz until there is a mode */
